speechtext:
When we realize that
every dollar of the money is expended by, and every day's work done under the supervision of, the Provincial Government's offi-'cers, we see how difficult it is for the Federal Government or the Federal officers to know that every dollar is being wisely spent. I do not agree with what some of my friends over here have said with regard to expenditures on good roads and the inadvisability of building so many roads, in favour of good roads throughout ario; I do not think we can have too y of them. But I think the minister Id impress upon his officials the neces-'or seeing that every dollar which is -on roads in Ontario, by the present vernment at least, be spent on what will uarn out to be permanent roads. It would be a crime against the people of this country, particularly against the people of Ontario, if millions and tens of millions of dollars are spent during the next few years on roads that will have to be rebuilt
in the course of another ten or twelve years. That is what the result has been in connection with the money spent under the county system during the last fifteen years;
